WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.100 --> 00:06.880
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

3
00:09.010 --> 00:12.860
[Adapted from the webtoon "The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

4
00:12.860 --> 00:15.640
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

5
00:15.640 --> 00:18.560
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

6
00:35.000 --> 00:36.610
[Yoo Dohyun]

7
00:36.620 --> 00:38.230
[Cho Chanhyeon]

8
00:38.350 --> 00:39.930
[Ko Gyeol]

9
00:41.440 --> 00:44.890
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

10
00:45.080 --> 00:49.890
[This series contains scenes of violence, self-harm, and potential triggers. Viewer discretion is advised.]

11
00:56.160 --> 00:57.970
Everyone is willing to provide testimony,

12
00:57.970 --> 00:59.970
but no one wants to testify in court.

13
01:00.430 --> 01:02.690
They're all afraid of being implicated.

14
01:04.129 --> 01:06.280
I've found the borrowed-name companies,

15
01:06.280 --> 01:09.000
but they all have figurehead bosses.

16
01:09.170 --> 01:12.190
There's no direct connection to the boss.

17
01:12.710 --> 01:15.400
I've also gone through the company's internal documents,

18
01:15.400 --> 01:17.440
but the books are suspiciously clean.

19
01:17.440 --> 01:19.570
Boss's name doesn't appear anywhere.

20
01:19.680 --> 01:21.480
Everything is signed by Lee Won.

21
01:22.060 --> 01:24.100
We can't turn the tables with just this.

22
01:24.100 --> 01:25.550
These are all just signs.

23
01:43.100 --> 01:45.850
[You have to sing, Hanyul.]

24
01:43.150 --> 01:44.500
You have to sing,

25
01:44.710 --> 01:45.910
Hanyul.

26
01:49.280 --> 01:50.900
Run away with me.

27
01:51.860 --> 01:52.979
What?

28
01:53.420 --> 01:55.250
I said let's run away together—

29
01:55.830 --> 01:57.380
to somewhere far away.

30
01:58.670 --> 02:00.750
To a place where no one can find us.

31
02:34.320 --> 02:35.560
Your birthday?

32
02:43.150 --> 02:45.410
The last few digits of your phone number?

33
02:52.970 --> 02:55.260
It must be related to you.

34
03:04.800 --> 03:06.000
What?

35
03:06.790 --> 03:08.130
What was it?

36
03:10.440 --> 03:11.950
My debut date.

37
03:12.950 --> 03:14.550
Lee Won is really something.

38
03:23.730 --> 03:25.050
But why are we here?

39
03:25.710 --> 03:28.440
I thought there might be something helpful here.

40
03:37.410 --> 03:40.280
True, Lee Won is definitely not a simple guy.

41
03:42.500 --> 03:45.630
There must be some evidence hidden behind this.

42
03:47.200 --> 03:50.460
But he couldn't do anything in front of the boss.

43
03:50.710 --> 03:53.110
Could it be that they have something on him?

44
03:53.329 --> 03:57.100
It seems he's turning himself in to take all the blame.

45
03:58.120 --> 03:59.430
Why?

46
04:01.270 --> 04:02.570
Why did he do that?

47
04:08.160 --> 04:10.060
Do you have any clues?

48
04:22.700 --> 04:25.760
[Collateral Contract]

49
04:24.290 --> 04:25.610
Found it.

50
04:32.780 --> 04:34.340
Collateral contract?

51
04:34.720 --> 04:38.040
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

52
04:45.630 --> 04:47.409
Hey, are you two out?

53
04:47.640 --> 04:48.260
Yes.

54
04:48.420 --> 04:49.360
Where are you?

55
04:50.140 --> 04:51.760
Hanyul and I came to Lee Won's house.

56
04:51.760 --> 04:53.760
Lee Won's house? Seriously.

57
04:54.070 --> 04:55.800
We did find something, though.

58
04:55.900 --> 04:57.700
What? Did you get anything?

59
04:57.840 --> 04:59.710
Not anything to completely turn the tables.

60
04:59.710 --> 05:00.800
What is it?

61
05:01.050 --> 05:02.970
But we can try some other way.

62
05:03.100 --> 05:04.250
Damn it, what is it?

63
05:04.390 --> 05:06.120
We found a special contract.

64
05:06.350 --> 05:07.460
Contract?

65
05:08.360 --> 05:12.370
I'm going to the Chairman's office to look for a similar contract.

66
05:12.520 --> 05:14.640
Okay, I got it.

67
05:16.890 --> 05:19.640
Before Lee Hanyul comes of age,

68
05:19.700 --> 05:23.140
Lee Won will repay all of Lee Hanyul's debts and interest on his behalf.

69
05:23.140 --> 05:24.540
During this period,

70
05:24.700 --> 05:29.100
the creditor waives all personal and legal rights over Lee Hanyul.

71
05:33.080 --> 05:34.140
Come here.

72
05:34.440 --> 05:35.400
Let me go!

73
05:35.700 --> 05:37.570
Hey, you go.

74
05:38.080 --> 05:39.400
Hurry up and go!

75
05:39.590 --> 05:40.610
Mom.

76
05:40.990 --> 05:42.159
Mom!

77
05:42.300 --> 05:43.159
Mom!

78
05:43.430 --> 05:44.990
Don't ever come back.

79
05:49.420 --> 05:51.540
That person back then was you.

80
05:56.440 --> 05:59.950
If Lee Hanyul does not return after coming of age,

81
06:00.080 --> 06:02.330
500 times the interest will be added to the original debt,

82
06:02.330 --> 06:04.010
and all debts

83
06:05.130 --> 06:06.930
will be repaid by Lee Won himself

84
06:07.440 --> 06:09.390
in full.

85
06:09.230 --> 06:11.750
[Signature: Lee Won]

86
06:12.650 --> 06:14.230
Why on earth?

87
06:24.700 --> 06:30.960
[A child abandoned by his parents for just some money]

88
06:27.510 --> 06:30.730
A child abandoned by his parents for just some money...

89
06:35.930 --> 06:37.690
A child who looked so much like me

90
06:37.690 --> 06:40.750
when I was crying alone as a kid.

91
06:46.570 --> 06:48.140
I was curious

92
06:48.720 --> 06:50.840
if you could live a different life from me

93
06:50.840 --> 06:52.720
escaping this place.

94
06:56.140 --> 06:59.040
Since I couldn't be saved,

95
06:59.170 --> 07:01.270
I thought I could at least live a different life

96
07:01.270 --> 07:03.550
through you.

97
07:16.630 --> 07:17.740
That day,

98
07:18.740 --> 07:21.840
I heard your singing for the first time.

99
07:23.530 --> 07:25.460
And for the first time,

100
07:26.500 --> 07:28.550
I had something I wanted to do.

101
07:30.090 --> 07:32.150
I wanted to write songs

102
07:33.020 --> 07:35.400
for you.

103
07:39.770 --> 07:42.710
To me, who was already trapped in the gutter,

104
07:42.840 --> 07:45.380
this dream was too whimsical—

105
07:45.520 --> 07:48.330
something I didn't deserve to have.

106
08:01.670 --> 08:03.180
Where are you, rascal?

107
08:03.340 --> 08:04.420
Get back here.

108
08:04.580 --> 08:05.670
Yes, understood.

109
08:06.210 --> 08:07.060
Yes.

110
08:29.940 --> 08:33.890
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

111
08:33.520 --> 08:35.700
-You have to sing, Hanyul. -You have to sing, Hanyul.

112
08:33.929 --> 08:36.880
[You have to sing, Hanyul.]

113
09:09.410 --> 09:10.890
Using young children as collateral,

114
09:10.890 --> 09:13.500
the so-called "child collateral loan" syndicate, which illegally lent hundreds of millions of won,

115
09:13.500 --> 09:17.570
has been arrested by the prosecution.

116
09:17.150 --> 09:22.740
[Defaulting parents; Forced placement into criminal syndicates; Trained as organization members]

117
09:17.890 --> 09:21.070
It is reported that after forcibly taking custody of young children

118
09:21.070 --> 09:23.150
from parents unable to pay their debts,

119
09:23.150 --> 09:25.650
they would forcibly entrust them to criminal syndicates

120
09:25.650 --> 09:29.610
to train them as gang members for future criminal offenses.

121
09:30.250 --> 09:33.980
These bastards are worse than animals.

122
09:34.100 --> 09:37.030
They should be punished down all their generations.

123
09:37.250 --> 09:38.650
Shockingly,

124
09:38.790 --> 09:40.010
this illegal organization

125
09:40.010 --> 09:43.250
belongs to the same company as the entertainment agency

126
09:43.380 --> 09:48.310
that recently caused an uproar over a tens-of-billions-of-won money laundering case.

127
09:49.140 --> 09:50.700
But Hanyul,

128
09:51.070 --> 09:53.330
if it weren't for Won,

129
09:53.450 --> 09:57.380
you'd be holding a knife right now instead of a microphone.

130
10:00.750 --> 10:04.070
Also, Won sent a message, so don't worry too much.

131
10:05.850 --> 10:09.770
Speaking of which, Lee Won will probably be locked up for a whole year.

132
10:10.740 --> 10:12.950
Herod, you brat...

133
10:13.210 --> 10:16.590
Why do you sound so happy and not worried at all?

134
10:17.180 --> 10:18.570
I am worried.

135
10:18.710 --> 10:19.650
You brat.

136
10:21.160 --> 10:24.820
A sincere voice should come from the heart.

137
10:25.070 --> 10:27.390
I won't be able to sing anymore anyway.

138
10:27.540 --> 10:29.100
Whose fault is that?

139
10:29.220 --> 10:32.130
Who told you to be so despicable as to steal someone else's song?

140
10:32.130 --> 10:33.130
Hanyul,

141
10:33.270 --> 10:35.080
do you want to sign directly with our company?

142
10:35.080 --> 10:36.140
What?

143
10:36.600 --> 10:39.000
Isn't that piggybacking on his success?

144
10:39.600 --> 10:41.230
That won't do.

145
10:41.650 --> 10:43.580
You know that people who just retired from the front lines

146
10:43.580 --> 10:45.640
are more sensitive to trends, right?

147
10:46.120 --> 10:47.280
Hanyul,

148
10:47.890 --> 10:49.550
don't overthink it, just go with me...

149
10:49.550 --> 10:51.930
You brat, you criminal.

150
10:52.050 --> 10:53.630
Believe it or not, I'll give you a karate chop.

151
10:53.630 --> 10:54.700
Hanyul, you choose.

152
10:54.700 --> 10:56.100
Who do you want to go with?

153
10:58.320 --> 11:00.450
I just want to sing.

154
11:02.920 --> 11:04.580
I want to sing.

155
11:06.970 --> 11:09.730
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

156
11:18.960 --> 11:21.490
With the sound of sugar cubes dropping,

157
11:21.740 --> 11:23.190
my heart...

158
11:28.370 --> 11:31.030
Herod, are you really not going to sing anymore?

159
11:31.630 --> 11:33.500
I just feel like this isn't right.

160
11:33.770 --> 11:35.910
You've practiced so much.

161
11:36.550 --> 11:38.160
How can I have the nerve to sing this song?

162
11:38.160 --> 11:39.630
There too?

163
11:41.910 --> 11:43.020
I'm leaving.

164
11:45.570 --> 11:46.660
Hey, Herod.

165
11:47.820 --> 11:48.870
Why?

166
11:49.410 --> 11:51.490
Why not use that nice practice room

167
11:51.610 --> 11:53.290
and insist on coming here to practice?

168
11:53.290 --> 11:54.240
Seriously.

169
11:58.420 --> 11:59.850
Is the practice going well?

170
11:59.850 --> 12:01.200
Yeah, I guess.

171
12:02.260 --> 12:04.270
Time flies so fast.

172
12:04.970 --> 12:07.780
Hanyul's concert is less than a week away.

173
12:08.150 --> 12:09.550
I mean, what rookie singer

174
12:09.550 --> 12:12.030
would hold a concert right after their official debut?

175
12:12.030 --> 12:14.360
How many seats does that venue have again?

176
12:14.970 --> 12:16.900
Lee Won is really going overboard.

177
12:17.620 --> 12:19.200
Brat.

178
12:20.080 --> 12:23.080
The pre-released "The Sound of Sugar Cubes" was a hit.

179
12:23.190 --> 12:24.850
They say he even has a fan club.

180
12:24.940 --> 12:27.290
Right, the fan club is called

181
12:27.410 --> 12:28.220
Yulmu-cha—

182
12:28.330 --> 12:29.840
no, oxblood soup (Seonjit-guk).

183
12:29.840 --> 12:31.340
It's called Melody (Seonyul).

184
12:31.340 --> 12:33.560
Right, I know. I know.

185
12:33.780 --> 12:35.820
I also know the fans' nickname. It's...

186
12:35.820 --> 12:36.680
Seasoned Salt.

187
12:36.750 --> 12:37.750
Seasoning.

188
12:38.160 --> 12:39.790
It's Sugar.

189
12:40.320 --> 12:42.730
Brat, how do you know so much?

190
12:42.890 --> 12:44.540
He's a fan of Hanyul.

191
12:47.790 --> 12:48.890
All right.

192
12:49.550 --> 12:51.050
Then let's listen to this song.

193
12:51.050 --> 12:52.180
Composed by Adolph.

194
12:52.180 --> 12:53.330
Sung by Lee Hanyul and Herod.

195
12:53.330 --> 12:55.930
Title, "Sound of Dawn."

196
12:56.070 --> 12:57.370
Drop the beat!

197
13:01.610 --> 13:02.780
I can't sing it.

198
13:04.080 --> 13:04.940
Brat.

199
13:05.130 --> 13:07.010
You can't or don't want to sing?

200
13:08.240 --> 13:09.870
Who would want to see me back on stage

201
13:09.870 --> 13:12.460
singing the song I stole from a friend?

202
13:12.750 --> 13:13.840
Don't you think?

203
13:22.050 --> 13:23.490
For me.

204
13:26.410 --> 13:28.780
Sing it for me, Herod.

205
13:30.180 --> 13:32.280
We were too young back then—

206
13:32.440 --> 13:34.040
too immature.

207
13:34.700 --> 13:37.830
Things went completely differently than we expected.

208
13:38.790 --> 13:43.460
I don't want to waste any more time on hatred.

209
13:45.080 --> 13:47.060
So let's just look forward.

210
13:47.840 --> 13:50.350
Don't look back, just look forward.

211
13:51.900 --> 13:54.140
The song you took from me,

212
13:55.060 --> 13:56.880
you can give it back to me.

213
13:59.800 --> 14:01.380
You guys sing it.

214
14:03.100 --> 14:04.860
You guys finish it.

215
14:30.610 --> 14:33.030
If you're listening,

216
14:33.180 --> 14:36.500
please come back just once.

217
14:36.780 --> 14:43.490
I'm still living in that dawn.

218
14:44.050 --> 14:45.940
Today, I

219
14:46.210 --> 14:49.460
still cross the dawn,

220
14:51.490 --> 14:57.540
to call out to you once more.

221
15:02.350 --> 15:04.200
Thank you all.

222
15:08.890 --> 15:10.480
I used to

223
15:11.660 --> 15:13.790
deeply hate

224
15:14.970 --> 15:17.330
my voice

225
15:17.480 --> 15:19.470
and myself.

226
15:20.500 --> 15:22.940
So I chose to run away.

227
15:23.780 --> 15:27.120
I tried hard to erase myself.

228
15:28.620 --> 15:30.000
Later, I met a group of great friends.

229
15:30.000 --> 15:31.380
They made me realize

230
15:31.770 --> 15:33.670
that it's okay to run away.

231
15:33.840 --> 15:35.810
And that I can choose to run away.

232
15:37.150 --> 15:39.630
As long as I come back.

233
15:43.280 --> 15:45.810
The one who saved me from the world...

234
15:50.090 --> 15:52.550
who made me step out of my own little world...

235
15:54.620 --> 15:56.820
and the one who is by my side right now...

236
15:56.840 --> 15:59.780
I'm making you participate in Super Singer's audition.

237
15:59.780 --> 16:00.620
Honey water.

238
16:03.240 --> 16:05.520
You did nothing wrong.

239
16:08.590 --> 16:09.950
It was all you.

240
16:17.450 --> 16:20.550
The sound of it dropping

241
16:20.720 --> 16:23.870
makes me care for some reason.

242
16:24.150 --> 16:27.410
The moment you looked at me and smiled,

243
16:27.560 --> 16:29.520
time stopped.

244
16:31.510 --> 16:35.060
All the sunlight on the hem of your uniform,

245
16:35.210 --> 16:38.830
the faint smile in your pocket.

246
16:39.050 --> 16:41.920
I somehow called your name,

247
16:42.090 --> 16:45.470
and the breeze answered.

248
16:46.670 --> 16:50.330
It was just an ordinary day,

249
16:50.530 --> 16:54.310
but I don't know why it's so clear.

250
16:54.690 --> 17:00.830
I still remember the moment I suddenly looked at you.

251
17:02.710 --> 17:06.210
Those unspoken feelings

252
17:06.430 --> 17:10.510
melted in my mouth,

253
17:10.650 --> 17:17.480
disappearing piece by piece, making the memory sweeter.

254
17:17.800 --> 17:20.470
With the sound of sugar cubes dropping,

255
17:20.690 --> 17:24.329
my heart broke.

256
17:25.520 --> 17:28.690
My mouth is full of

257
17:28.890 --> 17:33.150
the season named after you.

258
17:33.330 --> 17:36.100
I thought even if it faded a little,

259
17:36.240 --> 17:39.780
it wouldn't matter.

260
17:39.930 --> 17:43.240
But why do I still act like this?

261
17:43.370 --> 17:47.720
I long for you to stay sweet.

262
17:48.660 --> 17:52.220
Leaning in a corner of the playground,

263
17:52.410 --> 17:56.470
it's like that song is only for you and me.

264
17:56.580 --> 17:59.760
Even if time takes everything away,

265
17:59.910 --> 18:02.930
only that fragrance remains.

266
18:04.060 --> 18:07.790
I tried to say I'm fine and smile,

267
18:07.980 --> 18:12.380
but actually, I'm not.

268
18:12.550 --> 18:15.160
Since the day I lost you,

269
18:15.300 --> 18:18.370
the season stopped.

270
18:20.210 --> 18:23.710
Those unspoken feelings

271
18:23.820 --> 18:27.870
melted in my mouth,

272
18:28.020 --> 18:34.840
disappearing piece by piece, making the memory sweeter.

273
18:35.020 --> 18:38.030
With the sound of sugar cubes dropping,

274
18:38.160 --> 18:41.570
my heart broke.

275
18:42.840 --> 18:46.210
My mouth is full of

276
18:46.350 --> 18:50.360
the season named after you.

277
18:50.560 --> 18:53.420
I thought even if it faded a little,

278
18:53.580 --> 18:57.230
it wouldn't matter.

279
18:57.440 --> 19:00.710
But why do I still act like this?

280
19:00.880 --> 19:04.810
I long for you to stay sweet.

281
19:06.730 --> 19:10.950
If one day we have the chance to meet again,

282
19:11.100 --> 19:14.930
will you smile as if nothing ever happened?

283
19:15.050 --> 19:19.100
I hope at least this time, I can say it—

284
19:19.270 --> 19:22.410
tell you

285
19:22.650 --> 19:25.500
all my feelings.

286
19:25.560 --> 19:28.340
With the sound of sugar cubes dropping,

287
19:28.480 --> 19:32.120
the world stopped.

288
19:33.200 --> 19:36.300
Just like the day you smiled,

289
19:36.560 --> 19:40.800
time also stopped.

290
19:40.950 --> 19:47.490
Everything is at the end of your white feelings.

291
19:47.650 --> 19:54.690
I'm still going to call out to you like this.

292
19:54.710 --> 19:58.560
Still, still.

293
20:02.770 --> 20:06.400
Still, that sound of the sugar cube is still here.

294
20:20.940 --> 20:22.090
I was upset.

295
20:23.620 --> 20:24.660
Hmm?

296
20:25.380 --> 20:26.440
What do you mean?

297
20:28.070 --> 20:30.070
That you left without saying a word.

298
20:30.690 --> 20:31.890
If I told you,

299
20:32.360 --> 20:34.040
would you have let me go?

300
20:35.280 --> 20:36.810
No, I wouldn't.

301
20:37.850 --> 20:40.770
But at least... I wouldn't have let you be alone.

302
20:41.370 --> 20:42.660
I know.

303
20:43.140 --> 20:45.010
That's why I left secretly.

304
20:45.730 --> 20:46.790
Tsk.

305
20:47.670 --> 20:48.700
Hey.

306
20:50.020 --> 20:52.630
I didn't even get to apologize to you properly.

307
20:53.810 --> 20:55.550
Nor thank you, either.

308
20:55.990 --> 20:58.170
You were trapped there because of me—

309
20:58.470 --> 21:00.760
under his control for the rest of your life,

310
21:00.760 --> 21:03.050
only able to take his orders.

311
21:05.460 --> 21:06.500
No.

312
21:09.530 --> 21:12.160
Thanks to you, I found something I wanted to do.

313
21:13.300 --> 21:15.790
I always hoped the songs you sang

314
21:15.970 --> 21:19.710
could be written by me.

315
21:21.060 --> 21:23.130
If it weren't for you,

316
21:23.470 --> 21:26.070
I probably would have been a punk my whole life.

317
21:27.160 --> 21:28.210
Tsk.

318
21:30.350 --> 21:32.750
Don't just disappear like that ever again.

319
21:33.400 --> 21:34.540
You too.

320
21:34.750 --> 21:35.750
Mm.

321
21:36.020 --> 21:36.920
Pinky swear.

322
21:37.090 --> 21:38.290
